stated_limits:
The unflagged changes are configuration truth plus logging/observability:
- executor default 40 -> 96;
- Serper fail-fast connect default 3.0 -> 8.0;
- start-command `env UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE="${UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE:-64}"` prefix;
- one `[loop] class=... uvloop=... UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE=...` INFO at startup;
- one `[STAGE] parse done elapsed_ms=<int> mode=llm|presplit|fallback` INFO per q-form parse (none on the explicit or vision paths);
- Bright Data: one ERROR per process per status (401/403) naming BRIGHTDATA_API_KEY, which becomes one Sentry event; the 401/403 WARNING body is withheld;
- /health gains `adapter_executor` {workers, queued} on every process that installed the pool, and `brightdata_auth` {last_status, at} only after a 401/403. The endpoint is public, so this exposure is deliberate (n6).

